If any current or future product candidate we develop receives marketing approval, whether as a single agent or in
combination with other therapies, it may nonetheless fail to gain sufficient market acceptance by physicians, patients, thirdparty payors, and others in the medical community. The degree of market acceptance of any product candidate, if approved
for commercial sale, will depend on a number of factors, including:
● efficacy and potential advantages compared to alternative treatments;
● the ability to offer our products, if approved, for sale at competitive prices;
